{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>לאדם, כל, גול, כל</b> — four words linked. <b>מערכי לב</b> (the arrangements of the heart): the thoughts that a man arranges in his heart; and from HaShem, the utterance of the tongue, for He brings it forth — for before the utterance we know it not, as in the matter of <i>אין מלה בלשוני</i> (there is no word on my tongue). And HaShem, who knows, and <b>מערכי לב</b> sees, <b>מענה איש</i> (a man's answer) — and this is <b>כל דרכי איש</b> (all a man's ways): though he be pure in his own eyes, HaShem sees his ways, for He weighs the spirits to do His will."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:05.877683451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}